# DBVO Dialogue Tweaks — the CONTROL for voiceboost.steps: slider at 100% must NOT boost.
#
# Same stage, same boot, same console stimulus as voiceboost.steps, with the slider at 1.0
# (100%). The DLL must leave the XAudio2 voice alone and write no "voice boost" line at all; the
# last step asserts that absence (a `!log:` gate fails fast if the line IS there).
#
#   SKYTEST_NO_AUTOLOAD=1 skytest replay ~/.cache/skytest-dbvotweaks \
#       mods/DBVODialogueTweaks/voiceboost-control.steps --headless --no-shots   # must PASS
#
# Together with voiceboost.steps this is the A/B on the slider semantics: the ONLY difference
# between the two scripts is the number in the papyrus-call args. See voiceboost.steps for why
# the probe (not the console) sets it and for the NO_AUTOLOAD note.

# --- boot: main menu -> the SkytestBase save (QASmoke) ------------------------------
click 1177 496          # CONTINUE — a coordinate click; a bare `enter` here is unreliable (#25)
wait 2s
tap enter               # "Continue from your last saved game?" -> Yes
wait 4s
click 602 409           # "Creations are currently loaded … continue?" -> Yes (#25). Harmless if absent.
wait until:inworld
wait 3s                 # inworld fires before the player's 3D settles (#16)

# --- slider at 100% = pass-through ----------------------------------------------------
cmd {"cmd":"papyrus-call","class":"DBVOTweaks","function":"SetPlayerVoiceVolume","args":[1.0]}
wait 1s

# --- speak the player's line ----------------------------------------------------------
tap tilde
wait until:menu:Console
type player.speaksound "dbvo/t1.fuz"
tap enter
cmd {"cmd":"status"}
tap tilde
wait until:!menu:Console

# --- THE ASSERTION: no boost line, ever, for this session -----------------------------
# 3 s is longer than the message round-trip to the audio thread by orders of magnitude; if a
# boost line were going to be written for this stimulus it exists by now.
wait 3s
wait until:!log:DBVODialogueTweaks|voice boost
